@startuml
title Authorisation and passport of a crypto-asset service provider (Articles 62 to 65)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF4F4
  ParticipantBorderColor #2F6F73
  LifeLineBorderColor #2F6F73
  ArrowColor #2F6F73
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2F6F73
}
participant "Applicant CASP" as C
participant "Home competent\nauthority" as NCA
participant "ESMA register\n(Art. 109)" as ESMA
participant "Host competent\nauthorities" as Host

C -> NCA : Application (Art. 62): programme of operations,\ncapital, governance, AML, ICT, segregation,\ncomplaints, service policies, continuity
NCA --> C : Acknowledgement within 5 working days
NCA -> NCA : Completeness check within 25 working days\n(deadline for missing items)
NCA --> C : Application complete
NCA -> NCA : Assessment within 40 working days\n(one suspension of at most 20)
NCA -> C : Reasoned decision listing the authorised\nservices, notified within 5 working days
NCA -> ESMA : Authorisation entered in the public register
note over C, NCA
  Conditions kept at all times (Art. 59(4));
  withdrawal if unused 12 months, dormant 9 months,
  irregular, non-compliant or AML failures (Art. 64)
end note
C -> NCA : Cross-border notification (Art. 65): target Member\nStates, services, start date, other activities
NCA -> Host : Forwarded within 10 working days,\nwith ESMA and EBA
NCA --> C : Confirmation of the forwarding
note over C
  Services may start on receipt of the confirmation,
  or at the latest 15 calendar days after submission
end note
@enduml
